    {
      "id": "33bbe609-757c-4f9a-a1b1-ea1761c5d50c",
      "name": "Sticky Note 893030b8",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2464,
        1072
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 0) Check the ticket is not already solved or closed\n\nRuns first, and on purpose does NOT post an internal note or reopen the ticket.\n\nWhy the guard: on 2026-07-23 Zendesk redelivered a ticket-created webhook 8h37m late. The automation re-ran on the original first email, found the refundable charges already consumed, and emailed the customer a refund rejection after having already granted the refund.\n\nWhy no internal note here: the shared Do not proceed path sets the ticket back to open. On a solved ticket that would re-queue it for agents and could re-fire the 2nd-message trigger.",
        "color": 3,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 300
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f20801fc-d204-4e94-90f7-506f1bbe3dec",
      "name": "Sticky Note 03d1b848",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        2720,
        560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1) Check for blocked emails",
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 120
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5f20343e-60e4-4450-8f80-e5c20aea1185",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3d6668b0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        3936,
        880
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2) One active ticket per requester\n\nActive = new, open, pending, hold. Solved and closed do NOT block - a returning customer with only resolved history is eligible for automation.\n\nCustom statuses (e.g. In Progress) report under their base status, so no config column is needed.\n\n**Keeper** = oldest active ticket (created_at asc). It proceeds.\n**Loser** = any other active ticket. It merges itself into the keeper and returns false, silently.\n\nOnly the loser acts on itself - the keeper never touches its siblings. That removes the race where two concurrent executions close each other.",
        "color": 4,
        "width": 430,
        "height": 260
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0d9e9bbb-8ab2-4ed3-a103-85c9e8d43126",
      "name": "Sticky Note e80fa8d5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        4992,
        912
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3) Check for contact form cancellations",
        "color": 7,
        "width": 230,
        "height": 120
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "cb7b284e-4980-4b1a-a608-fdbd4c997edb",
      "name": "Sticky Note 80cc5308",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        5760,
        576
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Do not proceed (loud)\nBlocked email / user not found / contact form cancellation / dedup disabled.\nInternal note + set to open + manual handling.",
